}

<section style="background-image:url('/assets/img/hiredevelopers/her2.webp'); background-repeat:no-repeat; background-size:cover; background-position:center;">
    <div class="container" data-aos="fade-up">
        <div class="row align-items-center">
            <div class="col-lg-8 mt-5">
                <h1 class="text-white text-start pt-5 pb-3"><b>MICROSOFT DYNAMICS 365 CRM CONSULTING</b></h1>
                <p class="text-white pb-4">Expert CRM Guidance</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="col-lg-7 text-center">
            @*  <img src="~/assets/img/hiredevelopers/DevImg.png" width="60%" height="60%" />*@
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-lg-8" style="text-align: justify;">
                <h2><b>Expert Dynamics 365 CRM Consulting</b></h2>
                <p>iFOX provides Dynamics 365 CRM consulting to help organizations assess their current processes, define practical CRM priorities, and prepare a solution that fits the way their teams work. Our approach connects business requirements with <a href="/dynamics-365-crm-services/Implementation">implementation readiness</a>, configuration advice, integration planning, user adoption, and ongoing improvement.</p>
                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Business Process Assessment: Review current workflows, information needs, roles, and pain points to identify where Dynamics 365 CRM can support more consistent and efficient work. The assessment creates a clear view of priorities for the next stage.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> CRM Strategy and Priorities: Translate business requirements into a practical Dynamics 365 CRM direction, including the processes, teams, data, and outcomes that should be addressed first.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Implementation Readiness: Review requirements, data readiness, integrations, security considerations, user roles, and adoption needs before configuration or implementation begins. This helps expose dependencies and open decisions early.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Configuration and Customization Advice: Recommend suitable forms, entities, dashboards, workflows, and business rules while distinguishing standard Dynamics 365 functionality from changes that require careful <a href="/dynamics-365-crm-services/Customization">customization</a> and, where relevant, Power Platform support.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> User Adoption Planning: Prepare role-relevant training and guidance around the processes users will follow, helping teams understand the CRM solution and use it effectively with the right <a href="/dynamics-365-crm-services/Power%20Platform">Power Platform</a> capabilities where appropriate.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="col-lg-4 Imgborder">
                <div><img src="/assets/img/dynamics365/businesswoman-discussing-with-disabled-woman.webp" class="img-fluid text-start ms-0 mb-5 mt-3 me-3 p-3" alt="Business professionals discussing a Dynamics 365 CRM strategy" /></div>
                <div><img src="/assets/img/dynamics365/representation-user-experience-interface-design-computer.webp" class="img-fluid text-start ms-0 mb-5 mt-3 me-3 p-3" alt="User experience interface for a Dynamics 365 CRM solution" /></div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section id="call-to-action" class="call-to-action section dark-background">
    <img src="/assets/img/dynamics365/office2.webp" alt="">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row aos-init aos-animate" data-aos="zoom-in" data-aos-delay="100">
            <div class="col-xl-9 text-center text-xl-start">
                <h3>Ready to assess your Dynamics 365 CRM needs?</h3>
                <p>Talk with iFOX about your current processes, implementation questions, and consulting priorities.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="col-xl-3 cta-btn-container text-center">
                <a class="cta-btn align-middle" href="/contact">Get Started</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-lg-4">
                <div><img src="/assets/img/dynamics365/representation-user-experience-interface-design-computer.webp" class="img-fluid text-start ms-0 mb-5 mt-3 me-3 p-3" alt="Dynamics 365 CRM user interface design" /></div>
            </div>
            <div class="col-lg-8 Imgborder" style="text-align: justify;">
                <h2><b>How Dynamics 365 CRM Consulting Supports Business Growth</b></h2>
                <p>A well-planned Dynamics 365 CRM environment should remain useful as business requirements change. Consulting can help teams make informed platform decisions, maintain trustworthy data, connect relevant systems, and improve adoption without losing sight of business priorities.</p>
                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Performance and Process Review: Review CRM usage, workflows, and business requirements to identify practical opportunities for improvement and clearer day-to-day operations.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Integration Guidance: Identify the business systems and applications that need to exchange information with Dynamics 365, then clarify data flows, ownership, and <a href="/dynamics-365-crm-services/Integration">integration considerations</a>.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Data Governance: Establish practical ownership, validation, access, and maintenance practices for CRM records and <a href="/dynamics-365-crm-services/Migration">data migration</a> so information remains accurate, consistent, and useful for reporting and customer operations.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Security and Role Planning: Align access, permissions, and user roles with organizational responsibilities so people can work with the information and functions relevant to their duties.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Business Benefits and Continuous Improvement: Use clearer processes, more reliable CRM data, connected information, and stronger user adoption as foundations for reviewing business needs and refining the Dynamics 365 solution over time with ongoing <a href="/dynamics-365-crm-services/Support">CRM support</a>.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section id="call-to-action-secondary" class="call-to-action section dark-background">
    <img src="/assets/img/dynamics365/office2.webp" alt="">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row aos-init aos-animate" data-aos="zoom-in" data-aos-delay="100">
            <div class="col-xl-9 text-center text-xl-start">
                <h3>Discuss your Dynamics 365 CRM consulting requirements</h3>
                <p>Contact iFOX to review your CRM processes, readiness questions, and priorities for a practical next step.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="col-xl-3 cta-btn-container text-center">
                <a class="cta-btn align-middle" href="/contact">Get Started</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
